From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:47:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: Emulate derivatives and implicit-LOD sampling in
 compute shaders.

Metal kernels have no air.dfdx/air.dfdy (pipeline creation refuses them), and
an implicit-LOD sample in a kernel read LOD 0. In a DXIL compute shader:

- DerivCoarseX..DerivFineY read the quad with air.quad_shuffle. The quad lane
  l is Metal's, the simd lane & 3: coarse x/y are lane 1 - lane 0 and lane 2 -
  lane 0; fine x/y are (l | 1) - (l & 2) and (l | 2) - (l & 1). 1D groups'
  quads (four consecutive group indices) are Metal's lane quads.
- Sample, SampleBias and SampleCmp take the quad's coarse gradients of their
  coordinates through the gradient path, scaled by 2^(sampler bias), SampleBias
  by 2^(bias + sampler bias); SampleCmp through the new comparison-gradient
  builder.
- CalculateLOD is 0.5 * log2(max(|ddx * size|^2, |ddy * size|^2)) from the
  coarse gradients and mip 0's size, the clamped one clamped to [0, mips - 1]
  of the view. Cubes keep Metal's LOD.
- AddWaveInputs defines the simd lane input for these ops.

Pixel shaders keep air.dfdx/air.dfdy and Metal's own LOD.

AIRBuilder::CreateSampleCmpGrad emits air.sample_compare_<depth kind>_grad
(texture, sampler, i32 1, coord, [slice], ref, ddx, ddy, clamp, [i1, offset],
i32 0); cubes take no offset.

Constant texel offsets of TextureLoad and the Sample family now wrap to D3D's
low 4 bits too, as runtime ones do: from Shader Model 6.7 DXC no longer checks
their range. The wrap is the identity on [-8, 7].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
